// PostMessageWithBody Post a message to a recipient.
//
// The sender is what the token names, so the body carries the recipient and nothing about who is sending. garam answers once the message is durably stored and does not check that the recipient exists: rejecting a message it cannot route would destroy it and tell the sender nothing, so a routing failure comes back later as an ordinary message instead (ADR-0013). The sender's idempotency key is what makes a retry store one message rather than two.
// Which recipients a sender may reach is two questions, and they are refused two different ways.
// Inside the sender's own organization, policy decides (ADR-0024): it reaches every recipient unless a policy attached to it says otherwise. A recipient a policy refuses is a 403 and nothing is stored, because garam could have routed the message and the organization said not to, so storing it would deliver what was refused.
// Across the organization boundary the precondition is a consent relation both organizations hold, which no policy reaches past (ADR-0035). Where that relation does not stand garam cannot route the message, so the post is stored and answered 201 like any other: what is stored is the refusal, addressed back to the sender as an ordinary inbound message whose sender is the recipient that could not be reached and whose body names the two organizations that do not both consent (ADR-0013). The 201 carries that refusal rather than the message submitted, which is how a caller tells the two apart, and its idempotency key derives from the sender's so a retried post is answered with the one refusal already stored.
// An agent presents its execution token here, which it holds once its execution has been activated (ADR-0118), and the call is admitted against the current activation and credential lineage in the transaction of its own write: after a replacement, a reassignment, a recovery or its agent token's expiry it is refused, on a connection already open too (ADR-0080). A missing execution token is 401, one that is not current, or one presented for an agent never activated, 403, and an agent token outside the agent's lineage, epoch or dates 409.
//
